</text>
Reason:
The bug occurs because the SIOCATMARK handler in unix_ioctl does not validate that the socket type is SOCK_STREAM. Since OOB (MSG_OOB) is only supported for SOCK_STREAM, allowing this ioctl on non-stream sockets (SOCK_DGRAM, SOCK_SEQPACKET) leads to incorrect behavior, such as operating on an uninitialized OOB state.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
